Reads both channels sequentially. Light percentage is inverted because the LDR divider outputs high voltage in the dark (high \(R_{LDR}\)) and low voltage in bright light (low \(R_{LDR}\)). Both readings are printed on a single UART line.

Moving Average Filter
/* USER CODE BEGIN PV */
#define FILTER_SIZE 8
uint16_t temp_buffer[FILTER_SIZE] = {0};
uint16_t light_buffer[FILTER_SIZE] = {0};
uint8_t filter_index = 0;
uint32_t temp_sum = 0, light_sum = 0;
/* USER CODE END PV */

uint16_t filter_update(uint16_t *buffer, uint32_t *sum,
                       uint16_t sample) {
    *sum -= buffer[filter_index];
    buffer[filter_index] = sample;
    *sum += sample;
    return *sum / FILTER_SIZE;
}

Circular buffer of 8 samples. Each call subtracts the oldest sample from the running sum, overwrites it with the new sample, adds it to the sum, and returns the average. O(1) per update — no need to re-sum the entire buffer.

Filtered Main Loop
while (1) {
    adc_temp_raw = read_adc_channel(0);
    uint16_t temp_filt = filter_update(
        temp_buffer, &temp_sum, adc_temp_raw);

    adc_light_raw = read_adc_channel(1);
    uint16_t light_filt = filter_update(
        light_buffer, &light_sum, adc_light_raw);

    filter_index = (filter_index + 1) % FILTER_SIZE;

    sprintf(uart_buf, "Raw: T=%4d L=%4d | Filt: T=%4d L=%4d\r\n",
            adc_temp_raw, adc_light_raw, temp_filt, light_filt);
    HAL_UART_Transmit(&huart2, (uint8_t *)uart_buf,
                      strlen(uart_buf), HAL_MAX_DELAY);
    HAL_Delay(100);
}

Prints both raw and filtered values side by side so you can compare. The filter_index wraps around with modulo — both channels share the same index since they’re sampled together. Delay is reduced to 100ms for faster visual feedback.

