Test 3: Deadlock Analysis
// Task A                         // Task B
osMutexAcquire(X, osWaitForever); osMutexAcquire(Y, osWaitForever);
osMutexAcquire(Y, osWaitForever); osMutexAcquire(X, osWaitForever);
osMutexRelease(Y);                osMutexRelease(X);
osMutexRelease(X);                osMutexRelease(Y);
Deadlock? Yes — Task A holds X, waits for Y. Task B holds Y, waits for X. Neither can proceed.
Fix: Always acquire mutexes in the same order (X → Y) in every task.

